{
  "requirement": "No prompt, tool result, or tool error the harness gives the model MUST state a\nline number or line range of a project source, except within source text it\nquotes and where a tool error repeats a line number the model supplied. The\nharness MUST identify a source location by file and outline selector under\n{cite}`requirements.references.outline_selectors` instead.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests adequately check `requirements.authoring.no_line_numbers`. I judged adequacy against the requirement text only. I read the implementation only to see where the error filter is applied.\n\n**Obligations**\n1. Tool results the model receives carry no line number or range. This covers reads, searches, outlines, reference listings and site matches.\n2. Tool errors carry none, except inside quoted source text and where an error repeats a number the model supplied.\n3. Prompts carry none.\n4. Locations are given by file and outline selector.\n\n**Tool results**\n- `src/authoring/tools.rs#mod[tests]/fn[reading_records_only_delivered_sources_and_their_terms]` checks that item reads have no `line_start` or `line_end`. It also checks that results of line-range reads, including a read through EOF, have no `line_end` and are identified by `item`. It checks that recorded inputs equal the outline input of file, selector and hash.\n- `.../fn[line_range_reads_record_the_innermost_covering_nodes]` checks that range-read results and recorded inputs have no line fields. It checks this for Rust nodes and for plain-text `line@hash` selectors.\n- `.../fn[search_merges_context_windows_and_respects_ignore_rules]` and `.../fn[separate_windows_in_one_node_are_divided_by_an_elision_line]` check that search entries and lines have no `line_start` or `line` keys. They check that an elision marker separates windows instead of line numbers.\n- `.../fn[outline_lists_nested_nodes_without_text_or_inputs]` checks that outline entries have only `item`, `kind`, `name` and `children`, and no `line_start`.\n- `.../fn[references_list_names_and_flattened_sites_without_recording_inputs]` uses whole-object equality on reference sites, which hold only name, role, file and item.\n\n**Tool errors**\n- `src/authoring/mod.rs#mod[tests]/fn[tool_errors_give_the_model_no_line_numbers_it_did_not_supply]` shows two things end to end through the conversation, where `dispatch` applies `without_source_lines`.\n  - A parse error whose raw text carries a source line reaches the model without it.\n  - A range error repeats only the start line the model supplied.\n- `src/authoring/line_numbers.rs#mod[tests]/fn[tool_errors_drop_the_source_line_of_a_parse_error]` covers several parse-position forms and rewrites each to the `file#` selector form. The forms are a parse-error line prefix, a line-and-column suffix, a file-position diagnostic prefix, and a second-position mention inside a duplicate-declaration error.\n- The same test keeps the model-supplied single-line and range forms of the range error unchanged. This covers the stated exception.\n\n**Prompts**\n- `.../fn[site_reviews_use_their_prompt_and_record_applies_and_the_site]` asserts that the whole site subject message equals the approved template filled with the file, selector and matches. The matches are `kind`, `query` and `item`, with no lines. It also asserts that the message reaches the model.\n- `.../fn[anchored_files_contribute_root_node_inputs]` asserts exact equality of the mandatory inputs, which use file, item, hash, kind and text and have no line fields.\n- `.../fn[submission_descriptions_explain_arguments_and_successful_completion]` asserts the submission tool descriptions require \"outline selectors\" and \"never line numbers\".\n- `src/sites.rs#mod[tests]/fn[sites_are_the_innermost_nodes_of_site_matches_and_violations_within_them]` asserts that `matches_value` yields kind, query, item and text only.\n\n**Residual risk**\n- There is no ast_grep-specific assertion. It uses the same shared `SearchNodes::entries` path as ripgrep, which is tested.\n- The `habeas` tool description includes an example call with line arguments. That is an argument example, not a statement of a project source location.\n\nNo requirement-violating behavior was found that these tests would accept, so I found no gap.",
  "references": "5f07d59d3d70ca6a503110d2a797133c2b9f1eafd54fb53e7ee2fb02587ec51a",
